WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.720
$4 million is what one Calgary board says a new flag rule would cost at schools. This is Omni View North America, episode 53. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. After that, the federal budget in Ottawa, unfinished Canada U.S. trade talks, and a New York plan for Rikers, then the California coast under the biggest waves in years. Alberta is rewriting a school flag rule before it takes effect in January 2027, CBC and the Philippine Canadian Inquirer Report.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:35.640
Because boards say many campuses have only one poll, and the rule wants the Canadian flag and the Alberta flag outdoors on two.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:44.880
Calgary's public board puts the extra polls at 223. Calgary Catholic expects 122 more at 20 to $30,000 a piece.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:50.820
Edmonton public says more than 170 sites need a poll. Edmonton Catholic counts 77.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:56.040
Education and Child Care Minister Demetrios Nicolites has told boards to wait on purchases

00:00:56.040 --> 00:01:00.480
while the province rewrites the guidelines so they do not carry costs he calls unnecessary.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.860
One option on the table is flying both flags indoors.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:08.880
The Alberta School Boards Association wants the rule suspended, citing money and local

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:09.340
control.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:14.020
Premier Danielle Smith said the government had not expected so many one-pole schools.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:18.480
The opposition new Democrats say board should have been consulted before the policy landed.

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:25.120
The same display rules also limit other flags on schoolgrounds, especially ones treated as political or ideological.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:31.359
Ottawa's Liberals have their 2026 budget through the House of Commons, Global News Reports.

00:01:31.959 --> 00:01:33.419
It was tabled on November 5.

00:01:33.979 --> 00:01:40.239
The paper says it sets out billions in new borrowing and tax measures aimed mostly at infrastructure and other capital projects.

00:01:40.679 --> 00:01:44.719
People who were in a meeting in China between Prime Minister Mark Carney and Donald Trump

00:01:44.719 --> 00:01:48.759
